(5857843, 849929, 32997, '<td valign="top">Am not sure what the point of this challenge was, but if I was voting I would say yours is certainly the most interesting and best in show...</td>', 'Am not sure what the point of this challenge was, but if I was voting I would say yours is certainly the most interesting and best in show...', '2010-02-07 22:21:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5857883, 848558, 107938, '<td valign="top">I really love the way the graffiti is so colorful in contrast with the ground, pillar, and roof.  You did an excellent job on a self-portrait, even in the weather and with nosy cops.</td>', 'I really love the way the graffiti is so colorful in contrast with the ground, pillar, and roof.  You did an excellent job on a self-portrait, even in the weather and with nosy cops.', '2010-02-07 22:38:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5858156, 849536, 114371, '<td valign="top">I like the composition.  Wish there was a bit more light (personal preference).  I have a few skateboard parks near my house.  I will try to emulate what you have done here.</td>', 'I like the composition.  Wish there was a bit more light (personal preference).  I have a few skateboard parks near my house.  I will try to emulate what you have done here.', '2010-02-08 01:03:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5858268, 850115, 90495, '<td valign="top">Yikes!</td>', 'Yikes!', '2010-02-08 02:34:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5858361, 849374, 28742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BlueRibbonGuy:</b></div><hr/><i>*For those wondering: this tunnel is on the east slope of Queen Anne Hill and feeds southbound Aurora Ave. into Dexter Ave.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Ahhh, thanks a bunch! I''ve been through there a few times.</td>', 'Originally posted by BlueRibbonGuy:*For those wondering: this tunnel is on the east slope of Queen Anne Hill and feeds southbound Aurora Ave. into Dexter Ave. Ahhh, thanks a bunch! I''ve been through there a few times.', '2010-02-08 04:07:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5859333, 850080, 105457, '<td valign="top">Hi Stephanie, greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First of all, welcome to our insane family of DPC :)<br/>You will have a lot of fun here, for sure!<br/> <br/>Regarding your photo:<br/> <br/>Composition / subject<br/>The subject you chose is really appealing and vibrant, you can feel the colours jump at you on the screen. However, the fact that you took the picture sideways takes much of the potential impact of it. The water meters add a new subject and point of interest, but they would be better if they were straight on.<br/> <br/>Processing<br/>Nicely done, minimal and effective, you really brought out the details in it.<br/> <br/>Overall <br/>A 36th place is a very good result, more being your second challenge.<br/>Keep them coming!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=105457" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">contact me</a>.<br/>Regards,<br/>Joao<br/></td>', 'Hi Stephanie, greetings from the Critique Club! First of all, welcome to our insane family of DPC :)You will have a lot of fun here, for sure! Regarding your photo: Composition / subjectThe subject you chose is really appealing and vibrant, you can feel the colours jump at you on the screen. However, the fact that you took the picture sideways takes much of the potential impact of it. The water meters add a new subject and point of interest, but they would be better if they were straight on. ProcessingNicely done, minimal and effective, you really brought out the details in it. Overall A 36th place is a very good result, more being your second challenge.Keep them coming! If you have any questions feel free to contact me.Regards,Joao', '2010-02-08 16:23:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5859533, 849557, 98339, '<td valign="top">this is down right cool...love the vivid colors...</td>', 'this is down right cool...love the vivid colors...', '2010-02-08 18:07:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868038, 849536, 52115, '<td valign="top">I really think this is excellent, combining the colorful grafitti with a silhouette against the sky. Riminds me of the ET movie riding a bicycle silhouetted against the sky, But combined with the color, makes it even better. Our Lakewood skatepark has no grafitti at all.<br/> <br/>I''d like to see the camera angle just a little more to the right and lower. To get body from waist up against the sky, and just a slight touch of spotlight on his skateboard-only by an assistent. A Lower angle would make him higher in the air, too. Yes flash, but only to emphasize the skateboard.</td>', 'I really think this is excellent, combining the colorful grafitti with a silhouette against the sky. Riminds me of the ET movie riding a bicycle silhouetted against the sky, But combined with the color, makes it even better. Our Lakewood skatepark has no grafitti at all. I''d like to see the camera angle just a little more to the right and lower. To get body from waist up against the sky, and just a slight touch of spotlight on his skateboard-only by an assistent. A Lower angle would make him higher in the air, too. Yes flash, but only to emphasize the skateboard.', '2010-02-15 13:28:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5875161, 849732, 68504, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Digipixer:</b></div><hr/><i> The people standing around arent interesting,crop them out and concentrate on the graffiti.There probably is more than you show in this pix. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah.  I know them.  Very boring peeps.  We need more writing on the wall!<br/> <br/>- message from your local clairvoyant/prophet.<br/> <br/>Golly gee, that little peeps strip gives that essential frisson of desire.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Digipixer: The people standing around arent interesting,crop them out and concentrate on the graffiti.There probably is more than you show in this pix.   Yeah.  I know them.  Very boring peeps.  We need more writing on the wall! - message from your local clairvoyant/prophet. Golly gee, that little peeps strip gives that essential frisson of desire.', '2010-02-21 15:27:08.000000', NULL, 0),
